    "result_text": "All tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner email support following the existing telephone normalization pattern.\n\n**Spec/DTO** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property to the `OwnerFields` schema in `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (not in `required`), so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain `getEmail`/`setEmail`.\n\n**Entity & persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java`: added an `email` column with getter/setter.\n- Added an `email` column to all four DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`), and appended a `NULL` email to the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb`/`mysql` `data.sql` (the `h2`/`postgres` inserts already use explicit column lists, so they were fine).\n\n**Validation/normalization function** (mirrors `NormalizeTelephone`)\n- `NormalizeEmail.java`: when `email` is absent/blank it's left alone; when present it's checked against a basic syntactic regex and either rejected via the checked `InvalidEmailException` or written back lower-cased onto the request DTO.\n- `InvalidEmailException.java` + `escalation/InvalidEmailExceptionHandler.java` + the escalation YAML \u2192 responds 400.\n- Wired `normalizeEmail` into both `owners.POST.yml` (after telephone normalization) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (after validate), under the same `transaction` governance.\n- `ApplyOwner.java`: now copies `email` onto the entity on update.\n\nThe mapper maps `email` automatically by name in both directions, so it's stored and returned lower-cased, invalid emails return 400, and a missing email is accepted \u2014 matching all three acceptance tests.",
